                <pb facs="0597" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg575"/>

                <head>No. 105.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to General Schenck</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-13"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 13,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Telegraph and write to Davis, Hotel Beau Rivage, Geneva, as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>See my telegrams to Schenck of second and ninth June. If arguments are
                            filed in good faith, without offensive notice, we will assent to their
                            motion for adjournment.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
